title the m1_smoke fixture, written as a tree

# This is the smoke's asymmetric fixture in .tree form: base holds
# /hello and /subdir/inner, onto adds /extra, off-of hard-links
# /hello2 onto /hello and edits the inner file.
#
# It exists to check the SUITE's arithmetic against numbers a real
# engine actually printed. The box reported, for exactly this shape:
#
#   walk pools base 4 onto 5 off-of 4, distinct names 6
#   name table 6 names, held base 4 onto 5 off-of 5
#   components 5 over 13 pools
#
# "treedump -c" prints what the suite would predict, so the input
# census can be verified here rather than only on a box. That matters
# because those predictions are what the first box run will use to
# decide whether the MATERIALIZER built the fixture correctly, and a
# prediction nobody has checked is not a check.
#
# No gold: the suite would skip this one, and the arithmetic is the
# whole point of it.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: hello = world
    3-100: subdir/
      4-100: inner = nested

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: hello = world
    3-100: subdir/
      4-100: inner = nested
    5-200: extra = x

tree offof
  1-1: /
    2-100: hello = world
    2-100: hello2
    3-100: subdir/
      4-100: inner = edited
